2. Not covered by this license
------------------------------
These files keep the license they have always had:

    models/nemo4.tnm            CC-BY-SA-4.0
    models/oido_stream.tnm      CC-BY-SA-4.0
    models/oido_v2a.tnm         CC-BY-SA-4.0
    models/oido_v2b.tnm         CC-BY-SA-4.0
    models/nemo_small/tokenizer.model   CC-BY-4.0 (NVIDIA's original tokenizer, not modified)

Why. The four CC-BY-SA-4.0 models were fine-tuned on data that includes OpenSLR 70 and 83 (CC-BY-SA-4.0) and
People's Speech (whose material is CC-BY or CC-BY-SA). Share-alike means the result has to be shared under
CC-BY-SA-4.0 too, so Lokutor cannot add a non-commercial restriction to them. They may be used commercially under the
terms of CC-BY-SA-4.0 (attribution, same license for adaptations). The tokenizer is NVIDIA's file, unchanged, so it keeps
NVIDIA's license.

Language models. The English models oido_v2a.tnm and oido_v2b.tnm are CC-BY-SA-4.0, but their language model
oido_v2.tlm is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The engine decodes without a language model (greedy decoding), at a higher word error
rate, so the CC-BY-SA models can be used commercially on their own.

